					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-11503691#post-4236797</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-11503691/speed-demon#post-4236797</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 03 May 2019 00:35:18 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>The Great Hippo</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3938622</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>As far as the continued expansion of speculative urban sci-fi/fantasy fiction in the Foundation-verse, I can't help but be a little skeptical. Part of me resists this, because part of me can't help but see it as yet another step away from the more restrained approach to the universe that I prefer.</p> <p>But&#8230; this is still stylish, fun, and &#8212; most importantly! &#8212; <em>character-driven</em>. Having read most of it already, I've had the pleasure of seeing your sense of restraint evolve; both in how you've finished it prior to posting, <em>and</em> in how you've refrained from allowing the spectacle to overshadow the characters. In short: It's a fun, wild story &#8212; one that ultimately cares more about its characters than its explosions.</p> <p>(it still has plenty of explosions, though!)</p> <p>I've said this already in chat, but I'll say it here, too: The amount of focus, creativity, and restraint on display here is something you should be proud of.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-11503691#post-4236194</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-11503691/speed-demon#post-4236194</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 02 May 2019 10:57:59 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Jekeled</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1349098</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>On all metrics-including characterization, plot, and raw <em>style</em>-this series ranks as among the best on the site. Works like this, <em>Acquisitions,</em> and <em>Antimemetics</em> raise the bar for future submissions and prove that the wiki can (and should) serve as a home for original, high-quality writing.</p> <p>Upvoted and recommended without reservation.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
